          "text": "The East Ward member returned unopposed was James Ellis, not James Elliott. The list of nominations (Derry Journal, 6 January 1909, and the Strabane Weekly News) prints \"James Elliott, agent\", but the Londonderry Standard reports Blair, Canavan, Ellis and Conroy returned unopposed after M'Devitt's withdrawal, the Strabane Weekly News names the one new member as Mr. James Ellis in place of Mr. Dillon, and James Ellis sat on the council at its annual meeting of January 1911 (Tyrone Constitution). He had won the East Ward in 1905 and lost a contest in January 1912, when this term ended. (Londonderry Standard, Londonderry Standard, 8 January 1909, p. 5)"
